  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent political discourse in Kenya has been marked by heightened tensions involving President William Ruto and his former deputy, Rigathi Gachagua. Reports indicate a cycle of public exchanges involving accusations of tribalism, personal attacks, and disputes over the treatment of young political leaders, with the President comparing his former deputy's conduct to biblical figures. Amidst these broader political conflicts, President Ruto has publicly addressed commentary surrounding his personal fashion choices, specifically his suits. Furthermore, the President has used recent public appearances to call for decorum among those seeking elective offices, emphasizing the necessity of avoiding violence and intimidation as campaign strategies. The climate remains characterized by intense public and media scrutiny as various stakeholders debate the direction of political leadership and the conduct of established government figures in the lead-up to future electoral cycles.",
